# Security headers for Cloudflare Pages (copied into build/web by Flutter).
# See .github/workflows/deploy-web.yml and docs/SECURITY.md.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy is enforced since 5 October 2026, after it ran
# report-only against the deployed site. What a signed-in session loads was
# checked: the app and its CanvasKit (self), the Firebase SDK and Flutter's
# fallback fonts (gstatic), Supabase (data, functions, storage), Firebase
# sign-in (googleapis, apis.google.com, the auth iframe). Remote pictures —
# logos, news images, Google profile photos — come through Liz's own proxy on
# supabase.co. A wrong CSP blanks a Flutter app entirely: anything new the
# page loads from elsewhere must be added here first.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://www.gstatic.com https://apis.google.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://*.supabase.co; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co wss://*.supabase.co https://www.gstatic.com https://fonts.gstatic.com https://*.googleapis.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-src https://liz-f5f93.firebaseapp.com https://accounts.google.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'

# The app shell changes with every deploy; everything it loads is
# content-hashed or versioned by the service worker.
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/flutter_bootstrap.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

# Makers embed these on their own sites. Rebuilt daily with the pages, so an
# hour's caching keeps "Rising on Liz" no more than an hour stale.
/badge/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: cross-origin
